course: dictionary
lesson: 7165
title: Perish: many meanings, one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Perish is a word with several meanings, so the clues around it matter. «Many sailors perished in the storm.» The storm is the clue. Perish here means to die, which is a formal word often used for accidents, disasters and war.
explain: Perish can also mean to rot or go bad. Milk and fish are called perishable goods because they go bad quickly. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: "The fish will go bad if it is left out" still makes sense, so this meaning fits.
explain: In UK chat, «perished» or «perishing» means very cold, as in «it's perishing out there». In The Wind in the Willows, someone says they «must be perished», which means frozen right through. Read the whole sentence and the story before you decide which meaning fits.
fact: Perish means to die, to rot or go bad, or (in UK chat) to be very cold.
fact: «Perish the thought» means "I hope that never happens".
fact: «Perishable goods» are foods like milk and fish that go bad quickly, so they must be kept cold.
fact: «Perishing cold» means freezing cold.
fact: Perish is a formal word for dying, often in an accident, disaster or war, so use it with care.
exercise: «Many sailors perished in the storm.» What does perished mean here? | *Died | Sailed home | Went off, like milk | Were very cold
exercise: Mum says, «It's perishing out there, so wrap up warm!» What does perishing mean? | Going bad | Very hot | *Freezing cold | Very dangerous
exercise: Milk and fish are called «perishable goods». Why must they be kept cold? | *They go bad quickly | They turn into rubber | They are too heavy to move | They are fine at any temperature
test: What does «perish the thought» mean? | The food is going bad | Let us think very hard about it | *I hope that never happens | Someone is about to die
test: «The old rubber band began to perish.» What does perish mean here? | To grow bigger | To be very happy | To sing loudly | *To rot and get old
exam: Which sentence means the food will go bad? | The food will perish the thought | *The milk will perish if it is left out in the heat | The milk will sing a happy song
